        {
          "record_id": "char_719cd0333a9840efa32e1870e223b939",
          "record_type": "character",
          "label": "Farovald",
          "resolution_status": "resolved"
        }
      ],
      "required_locations": [],
      "ending_state": "By the end of Book 1, Luca has transformed his 789 discovery into the first durable guardian practice and has begun transferring responsibility to Elia. Italus remains hidden and biologically unexplained to the wider world. The reader now knows Farovald by name, understands that he was directly altered in the 589 singularity, and understands that he is an exceptional non-lineage continuity witness who will protect the wider secrecy perimeter while Luca's descendants carry guardianship. Farovald is explicitly not a guardian and does not control succession. Later aliases, later interventions, full lifespan, and final-series fate remain unrevealed.",
      "handoff_to_next_book": "As Luca ages, the central problem shifts from protecting Italus himself to ensuring that protection can survive him. Elia has grown up close enough to Luca and Italus to recognize patterns in their lives without initially possessing the full burden of the secret. Luca begins the deliberate transfer of practical knowledge, secrecy expectations, and responsibility to his daughter. Book 1 closes with guardianship no longer belonging solely to Luca: the lineage has begun. Book 2 opens with Elia confronting what it means to inherit a duty she did not create and must now make her own.",
      "allowed_reveals": [
        "farovald-storm-fragment",
        "farovald-nerve-reflex",
        "farovald-unaging-face",
        "farovald-perimeter-pact"
      ],
